        "id": 9324,
        "name": "SuperRick",
        "username": "SuperRick",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/superrick/{size}/2705_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-26T04:09:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So we took on the dreamer today: Scholar, Unity, and Fanatic in the wild, wild west.&nbsp;</p><p>We thought we'd totally win the game because Fanatic set that shield up around the dreamer and she had End of Days in her hand.&nbsp; Scholar had some card that would let you pull a card out of your discard pile and put it on your deck again, so basically we could wipe the dreamer twice.&nbsp;<br><br>Well, we doddled (we're still noobs) around and tried to clean up the first set of projections on our own without the EoD card.&nbsp; We wanted to save the shield around the Dreamer and also not lose our ongoings.&nbsp; Bad move, it cost us because we&nbsp;never could get over the hump and we kept getting wittled down on damage.&nbsp; She dropped EoD, but then we had to get six projections up to do EoD again and win.&nbsp; We took three out and by then there were three others back up again and she was able to nuke them.&nbsp; We ended the game with Scholar having 6 HP, and Unity and Fanatic having 3 each.<br><br>I've fought and beat the Chairman and Iron Legacy now, and both times everyone on the board felt like it was COMPLETLY impossible to win, but somehow we did.&nbsp; When we fought the Dreamer it was completly opposite: we thought we couldn't lose but we ALMOST DID.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:40:05.040Z",
