        "raw": "<p>So we took on the dreamer today: Scholar, Unity, and Fanatic in the wild, wild west.&nbsp;</p><p>We thought we&#39;d totally win the game because Fanatic set that shield up around the dreamer and she had End of Days in her hand.&nbsp; Scholar had some card that would let you pull a card out of your discard pile and put it on your deck again, so basically we could wipe the dreamer twice.&nbsp;<br /><br />Well, we doddled (we&#39;re still noobs) around and tried to clean up the first set of projections on our own without the EoD card.&nbsp; We wanted to save the shield around the Dreamer and also not lose our ongoings.&nbsp; Bad move, it cost us because we&nbsp;never could get over the hump and we kept getting wittled down on damage.&nbsp; She dropped EoD, but then we had to get six projections up to do EoD again and win.&nbsp; We took three out and by then there were three others back up again and she was able to nuke them.&nbsp; We ended the game with Scholar having 6 HP, and Unity and Fanatic having 3 each.<br /><br />I&#39;ve fought and beat the Chairman and Iron Legacy now, and both times everyone on the board felt like it was COMPLETLY impossible to win, but somehow we did.&nbsp; When we fought the Dreamer it was completly opposite: we thought we couldn&#39;t lose but we ALMOST DID.</p>",
