      {
        "id": 87678,
        "name": "Braithwhite",
        "username": "Braithwhite",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/braithwhite/{size}/1854_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-29T18:48:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Odin\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/odin/48/2572_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Odin:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My whoops moment had to do with getting Ra set up with solar flare + staff + Imbued fire + Flesh of the sun god. i had two games where I just destroyed the villain and then i looked up the rules for solar flare and realized what just happened.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>A LOT of people (myself included) have made that mistake, especially with the older versions of the game. &nbsp;It was such a common misconception that Christopher made a specific ruling about situations like that (the infamous \"rule 15\" you may hear about from time to time). &nbsp;Solar Flares are still super fun, though!</p>",
